{"sid": "d53912c4-b8e1-4fb2-a797-2288d1f589e5", "uid": "60f25627-06b2-433d-8aec-656b3a45f6fc", "seq": 3, "ts": 1791173403.7199533, "plan_id": "d2871cc1-d320-4b82-a027-b05c763aefc9", "event": {"type": "user_message", "kind": "message", "content": "Create an Employee Dashboard for Support360 using the existing ticket data and security rules. The dashboard should show only tickets raised by the currently logged-in employee and include summary cards for Total, Open, Assigned, In Progress, Resolved, and Closed tickets, a ticket-status chart. Do not create duplicate tables or business logic, and do not allow employees to view other employees' tickets. Use the existing Support360 data model, relationships, status values, and row-level security. After implementation, deploy the dashboard and perform a live runtime test to verify the counts, chart, ticket list, employee filtering, and navigation buttons work correctly.", "client_id": "c-muupuheq-txy5yrgs", "device": null, "seq": 3}}
{"sid": "d53912c4-b8e1-4fb2-a797-2288d1f589e5", "uid": "60f25627-06b2-433d-8aec-656b3a45f6fc", "seq": 9, "ts": 1791173484.0104845, "plan_id": "d2871cc1-d320-4b82-a027-b05c763aefc9", "event": {"type": "agent_reply", "content": "**Here's my plan**\n\n1. Register and create 4 new employee-scoped KPI card visuals: Total Tickets, Assigned Tickets, In Progress Tickets, Closed Tickets — each counting SUPPORT360_TICKET rows filtered to RAISED_BY = current logged-in employee.\n2. Reuse the existing support360_my_open_tickets_count (Open) and support360_my_awaiting_confirmation_count (Resolved) cards, the existing support360_my_tickets_by_status chart, and the existing support360_my_active_tickets_grid ticket list — no duplicate tables or business logic.\n3. Update the application.json entry for support360_employee_dashboard to describe the full composition.\n4. Modify the existing support360_employee_dashboard model to compose all 6 cards + status chart + ticket list + navigation buttons, keeping the dashboard's row-level restriction to the current employee.", "seq": 9}}
